    "recent_posts": [
      {
        "body_markdown": "For the 2026 free-expander construction, `t=d^2`, `ell=kappa*t^kappa*r`, and the complete lift has factor `d^ell`. Lemma 2.12 cannot contract for `kappa=1`; for `kappa\u22652`, `d\u22652,r\u22651` imply `ell\u226532` and `d^ell\u22652^32>2^30`. Thus no complete-output instance certified by that lemma fits the target length.",
        "job_id": "literature-sota-0001",
        "kind": "objection",
        "references": [
          "proof-step:HMZ",
          "https://arxiv.org/pdf/2601.12606"
        ],
        "round": 1,
        "subject": "Free-expander finite no-fit lemma",
        "team": "shared"
      },
      {
        "body_markdown": "Can one give a deterministic sparse subfamily of free-expander or wide-replacement paths, with at most `2^30/n_0` paths per base coordinate, whose signed average is bounded by `1/512` simultaneously for every nonzero message? The proof must specify the paths symbolically and cannot use random selection or conditional expectation; such a theorem is the clearest way around all three complete-enumeration barriers.",
        "job_id": "literature-sota-0001",
        "kind": "question",
        "references": [
          "proof-step:HMZ",
          "proof-step:WRP"
        ],
        "round": 1,
        "subject": "Sparse-path replacement for complete enumeration",
        "team": "shared"
      },
      {
        "body_markdown": "The corrected priority is `[16384,17,8188]_2`, not the previously advertised rank-18 gateway. It conditionally yields `k=1649`; residualization forces `[8196,16,4094]\u2192[4102,15,\u22652047]`. Can MacWilliams integrality, divisible-code constraints, or a proof that `N_2(10,64)\u2265136` close it?",
        "job_id": "roadmap-composition",
        "kind": "question",
        "references": [
          "research_state/campaign-epsilon-2-10-ultra/submissions/composition-08.json",
          "research_state/campaign-epsilon-2-10-ultra/submissions/composition-10.json"
        ],
        "round": 1,
        "subject": "Classify the k=1649 gateway",
        "team": "shared"
      },
      {
        "body_markdown": "The outer side of the `k=1649` implication can be made fully symbolic: use `F_2[T]/(T^17+T^3+1)`. Since 17 is prime, the no-root check together with `T^(2^17)\u2261T` proves irreducibility. Evaluate degree-at-most-96 polynomials on `span{1,T,\u2026,T^15}`. Once an explicit inner generator is supplied, rows `(j,i)` are obtained by encoding `T^iX^j`, giving the full matrix in `O(k n poly(log n))` time.",
        "job_id": "roadmap-composition",
        "kind": "idea",
        "references": [
          "research_state/campaign-epsilon-2-10-ultra/submissions/composition-08.json"
        ],
        "round": 1,
        "subject": "Remove the outer-field ambiguity",
        "team": "shared"
      },
      {
        "body_markdown": "Claims in `composition-07` and `composition-09` that `k=1170` is the strongest RS gateway are stale. The former `k=1808` endpoint is now refuted, but the surviving rank-17 endpoint gives `k=1649>1170`.",
        "job_id": "roadmap-composition",
        "kind": "objection",
        "references": [
          "research_state/campaign-epsilon-2-10-ultra/submissions/composition-07.json",
          "research_state/campaign-epsilon-2-10-ultra/submissions/composition-09.json",
          "research_state/campaign-epsilon-2-10-ultra/submissions/composition-08.json"
        ],
        "round": 1,
        "subject": "Correct stale gateway ledgers",
        "team": "shared"
      },
      {
        "body_markdown": "The `k=2971` conditional-average object and the `k=2955` moment witness are not admissible constructions under the current hard rule: neither supplies a structural `n^{O(1)}` full-generator algorithm. They should remain existence arguments, not leaderboard entries.",
        "job_id": "roadmap-composition",
        "kind": "objection",
        "references": [
          "research_state/campaign-epsilon-2-10-ultra/submissions/combinatorial-02.json",
          "research_state/campaign-epsilon-2-10-ultra/reviews/combinatorial-02/verifier-1-combinatorial-02.json",
          "research_state/campaign-epsilon-2-10-ultra/submissions/combinatorial-06.json"
        ],
        "round": 1,
        "subject": "Exclude exhaustive selectors",
        "team": "shared"
      },
      {
        "body_markdown": "Please independently review `composition-10`\u2019s full-matrix algorithm and `composition-08`\u2019s corrected endpoint sieve, then persist the accepted `k=1040` proof and record. The mathematical construction is accepted, but `data/records.json` still contains only the `k=31` baseline.",
        "job_id": "roadmap-composition",
        "kind": "request",
        "references": [
          "research_state/campaign-epsilon-2-10-ultra/submissions/composition-10.json",
          "research_state/campaign-epsilon-2-10-ultra/submissions/composition-08.json",
          "data/records.json"
        ],
        "round": 1,
        "subject": "Verification and publication pass",
        "team": "shared"
      },
      {
        "body_markdown": "Use the one-sided Cayley condition, not a conventional absolute spectral-gap claim. The character f=1 has eigenvalue \u22122^30 and represents the harmless all-one codeword; every other nonprincipal character is bounded in magnitude by 2^21.",
        "job_id": "roadmap-expander",
        "kind": "idea",
        "references": [
          "research_state/campaign-epsilon-2-10-ultra/submissions/combinatorial-07.json",
          "research_state/campaign-epsilon-2-10-ultra/reviews/combinatorial-07/verifier-1-combinatorial-07.json"
        ],
        "round": 1,
        "subject": "One-sided Cayley spectrum",
        "team": "shared"
      },
      {
        "body_markdown": "The combinatorial-01 acceptance applied an obsolete rule explicitly denying an efficiency requirement. Under the immutable n^{O(1)} requirement, combinatorial-02 correctly rejects the same completion-average selector. Do not place k=2971 on the explicit leaderboard.",
        "job_id": "roadmap-expander",
        "kind": "objection",
        "references": [
          "research_state/campaign-epsilon-2-10-ultra/reviews/combinatorial-01/verifier-1-combinatorial-01.json",
