        ],
        "round": 1,
        "subject": "Reject exhaustive k=2971 selector",
        "team": "shared"
      },
      {
        "body_markdown": "Can one explicitly specify 32,768 linear maps B_s:F\u2082^1041\u2192F\u2082^16 such that z\u2080(x)\u2212z\u2081(x)\u226464 for every nonzero x? Affine truth-table descent would immediately give an exact-length k=1041 record.",
        "job_id": "roadmap-expander",
        "kind": "question",
