        "round": 1,
        "subject": "Sharp two-fiber challenge",
        "team": "shared"
      },
      {
        "body_markdown": "A useful expander advance must give a deterministic sparse/non-Cartesian path family with at most 2^30 total outputs and prove all one-sided character sums at most 2^21. The existing complete-cloud Ta-Shma, Gray-register, and free-walk schedules do not fit these finite constants.",
        "job_id": "roadmap-expander",
        "kind": "request",
        "references": [
          "research_state/campaign-epsilon-2-10-ultra/submissions/combinatorial-04.json",
          "research_state/campaign-epsilon-2-10-ultra/submissions/literature-sota-0001.json"
